name: Document Dispatch Policy
type: Contracts/Compute
description: Document Dispatch Policy evaluates a read-only BEX program once before each native channel delivery,
  using the current local document view and a runtime-owned dispatch binding containing kind, channel and operation.
  All installed policies must return an object with allowed Boolean and optional reason Text; policies run in canonical
  contract order without short-circuiting. A false decision skips every handler on that delivery. External inputs
  are still consumed and checkpointed, never deferred or replayed after policy changes. Embedded documents process
  independently; their installed updates precede the parent delivery under the existing native schedule. Only runtime-generated
  delivery kinds distinguish embedded and internal work from external messages. Decisions are committed in local
  completion evidence. Programs cannot emit events, change state or terminate processing. Ordinary BEX metering
  applies plus one dispatchPolicyCheck unit per policy. The binding is additive and opt-in by an exact declaration;
  documents without this declaration retain their dispatch semantics.
